course: dictionary
lesson: 4587
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You do not need to know every word to understand a text. When you meet a word, read the words around it. They are its context, and they leave clues.
explain: Look at this sentence: «Foxes hunt chickens because they are hungry; a stronger coop protects the hens better than anger.» A coop is where farm birds live, so hens are the birds kept in it.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A hen is a female chicken, but it can also be the female of other birds, like a hen pheasant. To choose the right meaning, swap it into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A hen is a female chicken, a farm bird that lays eggs.
fact: A hen can also be the female of some other birds, like a hen pheasant.
fact: The male chicken is called a rooster or a cockerel.
fact: A chick hatches from a hen's egg after about 21 days.
fact: A hen party, or hen night, is a party for a woman before her wedding.
exercise: «A hen's egg must be kept warm for about three weeks before the chick hatches.» What is a hen in this sentence? | *A female chicken, a farm bird that lays eggs | A male chicken | A young chick | A kind of cow
exercise: «In summer Sashko visits his granny's village, where there's a korOva (cow), a svynya (pig), a kurka (hen) and a pIven (rooster).» Which word in this sentence means rooster? | leleka | *pIven | svynya | korOva
exercise: Lily says, «We are going to a hen night on Saturday.» What does hen night mean? | *A party for a woman before her wedding | A dinner of roast chicken | A party for hens on the farm | A night spent with chickens in the coop
test: «Foxes hunt chickens because they are hungry; a stronger coop protects the hens better than anger.» Which word in this sentence is the plural of hen? | *hens | foxes | coop | better
test: «An ostrich egg is the largest egg of any living bird, about as heavy as 20 to 24 hen's eggs.» What is the ostrich egg compared with for weight? | A rooster's comb | A cow's milk | *Hen's eggs | A stork's nest
exam: Which sentence uses hen for a female bird that is not a chicken? | The rooster crowed at dawn | *The hen pheasant hid in the long grass | The hen laid an egg in the coop | Our hen night is on Saturday
